  "comment": "Property display position \u2014 the `pill` value (2026-11-26): `propertySchema.create`/`update` `display` gains `\"pill\"`, the fourth value-display position: the value rides a dedicated PILLS ROW under the block, rendered even when empty so the pill itself is the add/edit affordance (the owner's ask: scheduled/deadline dates as clickable pills). This fixture exercises the acceptance lifecycle on a scratch workspace: a datetime 'Follow-up' schema creates WITH display \"pill\", a select 'Stage' schema (two options) creates display-less then updates to \"pill\", and a boolean 'Channel' schema creates with \"pill\" \u2014 then the 'Follow-up' schema's display clears back to the panel default (present-null clears, the keep/clear contract). Every client applier must accept, persist, and round-trip the new value. (The reject shapes \u2014 an unknown display value \u2014 are parse-level strict-schema rejects pinned inline in the protocol suite, the established pattern.) LOCKSTEP-PENDING: GTK/Flutter validators/appliers converge in the same slice.",
